## Hard rules (a validator will reject the CV if any is broken)
1. TRUTH: use only facts from the candidate profile. Every experience/project bullet must list in `source_ids` the profile bullet id(s) it is based on. Never invent tools, responsibilities, metrics or scope.
2. NUMBERS: every number or percentage you write must appear in the cited source bullets (for the summary: anywhere in the profile). Do not round, sum, or convert numbers.
3. NEVER mention these terms anywhere: {{ redactions | tojson }}
4. NEVER use these unconfirmed keywords (or their translations) anywhere: {{ unconfirmed | tojson }}
5. Skills: list only skills present in the profile.
6. `experience[].experience_id` must be a profile experience id. Include every profile experience from the last {{ years_back }} years (chronology must have no unexplained gaps), most recent first. Roles irrelevant to the job get at most 1-2 short bullets.
7. Do not include contact details, dates, company names or locations for experiences — they are filled in automatically.

## ATS optimisation
- Mirror the job's exact keywords where the candidate truthfully has the skill; put the most relevant ones in the summary, the first bullets and the first skill group.
- `headline`: the job's title (or the closest truthful variant).
- `summary`: 3-4 sentences positioning the candidate for THIS job.
- Bullets start with a strong action verb, one line to two lines each, most job-relevant first. Recent relevant role: 5-8 bullets.
- `skills`: 3-6 groups, most relevant group first, 4-12 items each.
- `projects`: include only projects that strengthen this application (0-3), 1-2 bullets each.
- `education`, `certifications`, `languages`: from the profile, translated; omit clearly irrelevant items (e.g. unrelated vocational schools) only if the CV would otherwise exceed {{ max_pages }} page(s).
- `section_titles`: standard, ATS-recognised headings in {{ language_name }} (e.g. "Professional Summary", "Work Experience", "Projects", "Skills", "Education", "Certifications", "Languages").
- `target_keywords`: the job keywords you used verbatim in the CV.
- The CV must fit on {{ max_pages }} A4 page(s).
{% if max_pages == 1 %}

## ONE-PAGE CV (strict)
The whole CV must fit on ONE A4 page. Be ruthless about relevance:
- `summary`: 2 sentences max.
- Most recent relevant role: 4-5 bullets, one line each where possible. Second role: 2 bullets. Older roles: 0-1 bullet (keep the role entry itself so the chronology has no gaps).
- `projects`: at most 1, only if it directly supports this job; otherwise none.
- `skills`: 3 groups, max 8 items each, only job-relevant skills.
- `education`: degrees only, no notes. `certifications`: max 2, the most relevant.
- Merge related facts into one bullet rather than dropping key metrics.
